    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The blade tears the night wind asunder. The sharp clang of metal and the interrogative of the officer lunge as one at Reed.\nBut she doesn't listen. She can hear wails far sharper in the winds.\nShe knows there are defenseless Tarans shedding blood in this conflict, falling, right this moment.\nShe could call out the names of each and every one of those wailing. It was but a few hours ago—when she'd heard their voices sing the folksong of home."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Reed",
      "speakerToken": "avg_1020_reed2_1#2$1",
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "...She simply—cannot hear these cries."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Reed",
      "speakerToken": "avg_1020_reed2_1#4$1",
